{"id":"pr-1470-draft-marek-tree-root-serving","number":null,"title":"Note Commitment Tree Root Serving","status":"Draft","statusDetail":null,"category":"Network","owners":["Marek"],"created":"2026-11-18","license":"MIT","discussionsTo":null,"pullRequest":null,"kind":"proposal","format":"md","source":"https://github.com/zcash/zips/blob/6a5aab9f471b9fe909048a06c61633ebb4c38d5d/zips/draft-marek-tree-root-serving.md","official":"https://github.com/zcash/zips/pull/1470","updatedAt":"2026-11-19T17:17:04Z","summary":"This ZIP defines the service flag NODE_TREE_ROOTS and the messages gettreeroots and treeroots for the Zcash peer-to-peer protocol specified in ZIP 204. 4 With them, a node obtains the tree roots of a range of blocks from a peer, and checks…","words":1246,"digest":"cfe894087fc769d41599338f45d6d94b2417b26212276388573c75dafd7da1fd","headings":[{"id":"terminology","title":"Terminology","level":2},{"id":"abstract","title":"Abstract","level":2},{"id":"motivation","title":"Motivation","level":2},{"id":"specification","title":"Specification","level":2},{"id":"serviceflag","title":"Service Flag","level":3},{"id":"gettreeroots","title":"gettreeroots","level":3},{"id":"treeroots","title":"treeroots","level":3},{"id":"servingroots","title":"Serving Roots","level":3},{"id":"requestingroots","title":"Requesting Roots","level":3},{"id":"verifyingroots","title":"Verifying Roots","level":3},{"id":"peermisbehaviour","title":"Peer Misbehaviour","level":3},{"id":"deployment","title":"Deployment","level":3},{"id":"rationale","title":"Rationale","level":2},{"id":"securityandprivacyconsiderations","title":"Security and Privacy Considerations","level":2},{"id":"testvectors","title":"Test Vectors","level":2},{"id":"referenceimplementation","title":"Reference Implementation","level":2},{"id":"references","title":"References","level":2}],"body":[{"tag":"h2","children":["Terminology"],"id":"terminology"},{"tag":"p","children":["The key words “MUST”, “MUST NOT”, “SHOULD”, and “MAY” in this document are to be interpreted as described in BCP 14 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["1"],"id":"fnref1","href":"#fn1"}]}," when, and only when, they appear in all capitals."]},{"tag":"dl","children":[{"tag":"dt","children":["tree roots"]},{"tag":"dd","children":["The roots of the Sapling, Orchard, and Ironwood note commitment trees after a block. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["2"],"id":"fnref2","href":"#fn2"}]}," ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["3"],"id":"fnref3","href":"#fn3"}]}]}]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Abstract"],"id":"abstract"},{"tag":"p","children":["This ZIP defines the service flag ",{"tag":"code","children":["NODE_TREE_ROOTS"]}," and the messages ",{"tag":"code","children":["gettreeroots"]}," and ",{"tag":"code","children":["treeroots"]}," for the Zcash peer-to-peer protocol specified in ZIP 204. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["4"],"id":"fnref4","href":"#fn4"}]}," With them, a node obtains the tree roots of a range of blocks from a peer, and checks them against the block headers. A node syncing from checkpoints can then maintain its chain history tree without updating its note commitment trees."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Motivation"],"id":"motivation"},{"tag":"p","children":["The chain history tree commits to each block’s tree roots. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["5"],"id":"fnref5","href":"#fn5"}]}," During checkpoint sync, a node updates its note commitment trees only to obtain these roots, and the updates take most of the time it spends committing blocks with many shielded outputs."]},{"tag":"p","children":["Block headers commit to the roots, so any peer can supply them. The Version 2 P2P protocol draft ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["6"],"id":"fnref6","href":"#fn6"}]}," defines the same capability. This ZIP specifies it for the current protocol, so that it can be deployed without the rest of that draft."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Specification"],"id":"specification"},{"tag":"p","children":["All messages defined in this ZIP are serialized in the standard encoding for P2P messages. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["4"],"id":"fnref4:1","href":"#fn4"}]}]},{"tag":"h3","children":["Service Flag"],"id":"serviceflag"},{"tag":"p","children":["The service flag ",{"tag":"code","children":["NODE_TREE_ROOTS"]}," is defined as bit 3 (",{"tag":"code","children":["0x0000000000000008"]},"). A node MUST NOT send ",{"tag":"code","children":["gettreeroots"]}," to a peer that did not set it in its ",{"tag":"code","children":["version"]}," message."]},{"tag":"h3","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["gettreeroots"]}],"id":"gettreeroots"},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"code","children":["gettreeroots"]}," message is defined as a message where the ",{"tag":"code","children":["command"]}," field is ",{"tag":"code","children":["\"gettreeroots\""]},", with the following payload:"]},{"tag":"table","children":[{"tag":"thead","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"th","children":["Bytes"]},{"tag":"th","children":["Name"]},{"tag":"th","children":["Data Type"]},{"tag":"th","children":["Description"]}]}]},{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":["4"]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["startHeight"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["uint32"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":["Height of the first block."]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":["32"]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["finalHash"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["uint8[32]"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":["Hash of the last block, in the byte order of ",{"tag":"code","children":["hashPrevBlock"]},". ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["7"],"id":"fnref7","href":"#fn7"}]}]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":["4"]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["count"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["uint32"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":["Number of blocks."]}]}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["The message requests the tree roots of the blocks at heights ",{"tag":"code","children":["startHeight"]}," to ",{"tag":"code","children":["end = startHeight + count - 1"]},", computed without wrapping. A message with ",{"tag":"code","children":["count"]}," 0 or greater than 4,000 is malformed."]},{"tag":"h3","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["treeroots"]}],"id":"treeroots"},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"code","children":["treeroots"]}," message is defined as a message where the ",{"tag":"code","children":["command"]}," field is (NUL-padded) ",{"tag":"code","children":["\"treeroots\""]},", with the following payload:"]},{"tag":"table","children":[{"tag":"thead","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"th","children":["Bytes"]},{"tag":"th","children":["Name"]},{"tag":"th","children":["Data Type"]},{"tag":"th","children":["Description"]}]}]},{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":["1"]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["result"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["uint8"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":["0 for roots, 1 for a refusal."]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":["varies"]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["entriesCount"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["CompactSize"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":["Number of entries, present only if ",{"tag":"code","children":["result"]}," is 0."]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":["varies"]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["entries"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["TreeRoots[]"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":["Entries, present only if ",{"tag":"code","children":["result"]}," is 0."]}]}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["A ",{"tag":"code","children":["TreeRoots"]}," entry has the following format:"]},{"tag":"table","children":[{"tag":"thead","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"th","children":["Bytes"]},{"tag":"th","children":["Name"]},{"tag":"th","children":["Data Type"]},{"tag":"th","children":["Description"]}]}]},{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":["32"]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["saplingRoot"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["uint8[32]"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":["Sapling root, encoded as ",{"tag":"code","children":["anchorSapling"]},". ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["8"],"id":"fnref8","href":"#fn8"}]}]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":["32"]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["orchardRoot"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["uint8[32]"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":["Orchard root, encoded as ",{"tag":"code","children":["anchorOrchard"]},"."]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":["32"]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["ironwoodRoot"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["uint8[32]"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":["Ironwood root, encoded as ",{"tag":"code","children":["anchorIronwood"]},". ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["3"],"id":"fnref3:1","href":"#fn3"}]}]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":["1"]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["hasAuthDataRoot"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["uint8"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":["1 if ",{"tag":"code","children":["authDataRoot"]}," is present, otherwise 0."]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":["0 or 32"]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["authDataRoot"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["uint8[32]"]}]},{"tag":"td","children":["The next block’s ",{"tag":"code","children":["hashAuthDataRoot"]},". ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["9"],"id":"fnref9","href":"#fn9"}]}]}]}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["A message is malformed if ",{"tag":"code","children":["result"]}," or ",{"tag":"code","children":["hasAuthDataRoot"]}," is neither 0 nor 1, ",{"tag":"code","children":["entriesCount"]}," is greater than 4,000, or a root is not the canonical encoding of a field element."]},{"tag":"h3","children":["Serving Roots"],"id":"servingroots"},{"tag":"p","children":["A node that sets ",{"tag":"code","children":["NODE_TREE_ROOTS"]}," SHOULD answer each ",{"tag":"code","children":["gettreeroots"]}," with a ",{"tag":"code","children":["treeroots"]},", which is a refusal if it does not serve the request, and MUST NOT send any other ",{"tag":"code","children":["treeroots"]},"."]},{"tag":"p","children":["A node MUST NOT send entries unless its best chain has a block at height ",{"tag":"code","children":["end"]}," with hash ",{"tag":"code","children":["finalHash"]},". The entries MUST be the tree roots of at most ",{"tag":"code","children":["count"]}," consecutive blocks of that chain, starting at height ",{"tag":"code","children":["startHeight"]},". In the entry for height ",{"tag":"code","children":["h"]},", ",{"tag":"code","children":["authDataRoot"]}," MUST be present if and only if height ",{"tag":"code","children":["h + 1"]}," is at or after NU5 activation, and is then the ",{"tag":"code","children":["hashAuthDataRoot"]}," of that chain’s block at height ",{"tag":"code","children":["h + 1"]},"."]},{"tag":"p","children":["Computing ",{"tag":"code","children":["authDataRoot"]}," reads the next block, so a node SHOULD bound the block data it reads per request. A node that lacks a block it needs, or reaches that bound, sends fewer entries."]},{"tag":"h3","children":["Requesting Roots"],"id":"requestingroots"},{"tag":"p","children":["A node MUST NOT send ",{"tag":"code","children":["gettreeroots"]}," on a connection while an earlier one on that connection is unanswered, or after it stops waiting for an answer, since a late answer cannot be matched to its request."]},{"tag":"p","children":["A node MUST ignore a ",{"tag":"code","children":["treeroots"]}," received while no ",{"tag":"code","children":["gettreeroots"]}," is outstanding on the connection, MUST treat one with more than ",{"tag":"code","children":["count"]}," entries as malformed, and MUST treat one with no entries as a refusal."]},{"tag":"h3","children":["Verifying Roots"],"id":"verifyingroots"},{"tag":"p","children":["A node MUST NOT use the entry for the block at height ",{"tag":"code","children":["h"]}," unless it has authenticated that block and the header at height ",{"tag":"code","children":["h + 1"]},", for example against its checkpoints, and:"]},{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["the root of each pool whose network upgrade (Sapling, NU5, or NU6.3) is not active at height ",{"tag":"code","children":["h"]}," is the root of that pool’s empty tree;"]},{"tag":"li","children":["if ",{"tag":"code","children":["h"]}," is at or after Sapling activation and before Heartwood activation, ",{"tag":"code","children":["saplingRoot"]}," equals the block’s ",{"tag":"code","children":["hashFinalSaplingRoot"]}," ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["7"],"id":"fnref7:1","href":"#fn7"}]},"; and"]},{"tag":"li","children":["if ",{"tag":"code","children":["h + 1"]}," is at or after Heartwood activation, the header at height ",{"tag":"code","children":["h + 1"]}," commits to the ",{"tag":"code","children":["hashChainHistoryRoot"]}," of the chain history tree after the block, computed with the supplied roots as specified in ZIP 221 and ZIP 258 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["5"],"id":"fnref5:1","href":"#fn5"}]}," ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["10"],"id":"fnref10","href":"#fn10"}]},", or to all zero bytes if that header’s block activates Heartwood. If the commitment is ",{"tag":"code","children":["hashBlockCommitments"]},", it is computed with ",{"tag":"code","children":["authDataRoot"]},", which MUST be present, as ",{"tag":"code","children":["hashAuthDataRoot"]},". ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["9"],"id":"fnref9:1","href":"#fn9"}]}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["A node MUST still check the next block’s authorizing data root against the verified ",{"tag":"code","children":["authDataRoot"]},"; if they differ, the block is invalid, not the entry."]},{"tag":"h3","children":["Peer Misbehaviour"],"id":"peermisbehaviour"},{"tag":"p","children":["A node MUST NOT answer a malformed ",{"tag":"code","children":["gettreeroots"]}," with entries or use a malformed ",{"tag":"code","children":["treeroots"]},", and MAY treat either as it treats other malformed P2P messages. It MAY penalize a peer that sends an entry that fails the checks in [Verifying Roots]."]},{"tag":"h3","children":["Deployment"],"id":"deployment"},{"tag":"p","children":["This ZIP requires no network upgrade."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Rationale"],"id":"rationale"},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"code","children":["finalHash"]}," binds a request to the requester’s chain: a node on another chain refuses, instead of sending roots that fail verification. Refusals let the requester try another peer at once."]},{"tag":"p","children":["From NU5, a header commits to the preceding chain history tree together with its own block’s ",{"tag":"code","children":["hashAuthDataRoot"]},". ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["9"],"id":"fnref9:2","href":"#fn9"}]}," Sending that digest lets a node verify an entry before it has the next block, and tell an invalid entry from an invalid block."]},{"tag":"p","children":["Bit 3 matches the Version 2 P2P protocol draft ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["6"],"id":"fnref6:1","href":"#fn6"}]},", so a node can advertise the same capability in both protocols."]},{"tag":"p","children":["4,000 entries take at most 516,004 bytes, within the 2 MiB message size limit. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["4"],"id":"fnref4:2","href":"#fn4"}]}]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Security and Privacy Considerations"],"id":"securityandprivacyconsiderations"},{"tag":"p","children":["A node uses an entry only after checking it against authenticated headers, so a peer can only withhold or delay roots. A node that has stopped updating its note commitment trees depends on peers serving roots until it obtains the trees by other means."]},{"tag":"p","children":["A request does not bind the block at height ",{"tag":"code","children":["end + 1"]},", so a peer whose best chain diverges there can send an entry for height ",{"tag":"code","children":["end"]}," that fails the checks, and be penalized."]},{"tag":"p","children":["A request reveals which heights a node is syncing, as ",{"tag":"code","children":["getheaders"]}," and ",{"tag":"code","children":["getdata"]}," do."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Test Vectors"],"id":"testvectors"},{"tag":"p","children":["The hashes and roots below are arbitrary bytes, except for the empty-tree roots."]},{"tag":"p","children":["A ",{"tag":"code","children":["gettreeroots"]}," payload for 2 blocks from height 100,000, with ",{"tag":"code","children":["finalHash"]}," bytes ",{"tag":"code","children":["00"]}," to ",{"tag":"code","children":["1f"]},":"]},{"tag":"pre","children":["a0860100\n000102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f101112131415161718191a1b1c1d1e1f\n02000000"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A ",{"tag":"code","children":["treeroots"]}," payload with one entry of the empty-tree roots and no ",{"tag":"code","children":["authDataRoot"]},":"]},{"tag":"pre","children":["00 01\nfbc2f4300c01f0b7820d00e3347c8da4ee614674376cbc45359daa54f9b5493e\nae2935f1dfd8a24aed7c70df7de3a668eb7a49b1319880dde2bbd9031ae5d82f\nae2935f1dfd8a24aed7c70df7de3a668eb7a49b1319880dde2bbd9031ae5d82f\n00"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A ",{"tag":"code","children":["treeroots"]}," payload with one entry of roots of bytes ",{"tag":"code","children":["01"]},", ",{"tag":"code","children":["02"]},", and ",{"tag":"code","children":["03"]},", and ",{"tag":"code","children":["authDataRoot"]}," bytes ",{"tag":"code","children":["04"]},":"]},{"tag":"pre","children":["00 01\n0101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101\n0202020202020202020202020202020202020202020202020202020202020202\n0303030303030303030303030303030303030303030303030303030303030303\n01\n0404040404040404040404040404040404040404040404040404040404040404"]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Reference Implementation"],"id":"referenceimplementation"},{"tag":"p","children":["Zebra serves tree roots, and uses them for checkpoint sync with the option ",{"tag":"code","children":["fast_tree_sync"]},". ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["11"],"id":"fnref11","href":"#fn11"}]}," Its handling of timed-out requests does not yet conform to [Requesting Roots]."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["References"],"id":"references"},{"tag":"hr","children":[]},{"tag":"ol","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Information on BCP 14 — “RFC 2119: Key words for use in RFCs to Indicate Requirement Levels” and “RFC 8174: Ambiguity of Uppercase vs Lowercase in RFC 2119 Key Words”"],"href":"https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/bcp14"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref1"}]}],"id":"fn1"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Zcash Protocol Specification, Version 2026.8.0 [NU6.3] or later"],"href":"https://zips.z.cash/protocol/protocol.pdf"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref2"}]}],"id":"fn2"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ZIP 229: Version 6 Transaction Format"],"href":"?view=governance&section=zips&record=zip-0229"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref3"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref3:1"}]}],"id":"fn3"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ZIP 204: Zcash P2P Network Protocol"],"href":"?view=governance&section=zips&record=zip-0204"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref4"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"hre